{"kind":"artifact","text":"The layer contract records the configuration bound as a mechanism, and keeps the citation guard as a property. Exact clean pushed head 5f2251157cdc0983500b6f0f41c8dfadc8428148 on request/repo-remote-link; tree 52206343, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's repair child 6631aeeb and my promise d38a434a.\n\nWHAT IS ADDED. The configuration contract for the Git commands this layer runs: every inherited GIT_CONFIG name is dropped and the isolation is set here rather than inherited. That is stated as a mechanism deliberately, alongside the existing routing-variable mechanism for the remote read, because both are guarantees about how a specific input is handled and there is no outcome to state in their place.\n\nWHAT IS DELIBERATELY LEFT AS A PROPERTY. The citation guard's paragraph is unchanged in kind: it still says the guard refuses whenever it cannot positively confirm that no live document cites the target, and that no list of variable names is load-bearing. Planner ruled that direction and it survives this head — the configuration bound narrows how an unanswerable lookup is reached and is still not what makes the answer safe.\n\nONE STALE EXAMPLE CORRECTED. That paragraph listed 'a hostile command-scope configuration' among the things that can stop the lookup. A caller can no longer reach command scope, so the list now reads a broken Git, a resource limit, or a setting in the repository's own configuration file. I made the parallel correction in internal/app/repo_remote_test.go, where a comment still claimed the fail-open was reachable by anyone who could put one variable in the resident's environment. Leaving either would have been a page describing a world this head changed.\n\nTHE TRADE IS ON THE PAGE, not only in the code. safe.directory is honoured only from protected configuration, so these commands refuse a repository owned by another user rather than consulting an operator allowance.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet and diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"5f2251157cdc0983500b6f0f41c8dfadc8428148","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}